\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Four nucleotides in DNA are:\par

\pard\fi568\li568\sl240\slmult1 A(Adenine),       T(Thymine),      G(Guanine),       C(Cytosine)\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 In DNA: (called Chargaff's Rule)\par

\pard\fi1136\sl240\slmult1 A always pair with T\par
G always pair with C\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Nitrogenous bases of opposite DNA strands held together by hydrogen bonds\par

\pard\fi1136\sl240\slmult1 A-T = 3 bonds                           G-C = 2 bonds\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 DNA has directionality\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1 DNA 'read' from 5 (phosphate backbone) to 3 (sugar backbone)\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul DNA Sequencing:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Working out the precise order of nucleotides in a DNA sample\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Sequence of DNA nucleotides determined using Sanger's method or gel electrophoresis\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi558\li720\sl240\slmult1 Uses dideoxyribonucleotides to stop lengthening of DNA strand\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Produces segments of different lengths be separated by gel electrophoresis\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul DNA Sequencing Uses:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Identifying inherited diseases\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Paternity/maternity tests\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Tracing ancestry\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Forensic science\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul Ethical Factors:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 These factors need to be considered when gaining and using genetic info\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Autonomy\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Confidentiality\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Equity\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Privacy\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction):\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Double-stranded DNA split into two single-stranded templates by heating it to 95 - 98\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Mixture cooled to 50 - 65. The primers bind (hybridise) to complementary strands of DNA\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Heating to 72 (optimum temp for TaqDNA polymerase) encourages synthesis of new DNA strands alongside templates\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Mixture heated again to separate newly-formed DNA strands from their partners\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Cycle of cooling and heating repeated\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}With each cycle (lasting around 2 mins) number of copies of template DNA is doubled\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}After 25 cycles, more than million DNA copies made\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul Gel Electrophoresis:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 First, a gel is cast from agarose - pure form of agar\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}At one end of gel are several (usually 8) small wells\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Invisible DNA fragments mixed with small volume of loading dye\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Dye dissolved in dense sugar solution, so when added, it sinks to bottom with DNA\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Buffer solution poured over gel. Ions in buffer solution conduct electricity. Buffer also stops gel drying out\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Current applied to electrodes, setting up electrical field across gel\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}DNA migrates through gel towards positive electrode\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Small fragments move quickly through porous gel - larger fragments travel more slowly\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Pieces of DNA separated by size\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Loading dye also moves through gel, progress of electrophoresis can be seen\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}After electrophoresis, gel stained to reveal DNA\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Either as smear (many fragments of wide range of sizes) or bands (each band comprised of numerous DNA fragments of similar size)\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul PCR Process:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Denaturing at 94 - breaks apart DNA strands\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Annealing at 60 - allows primer to bind to certain parts of sequence\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Extension 72 - DNA polymerase binds and DNA replication starts (longer strands made)\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}PCR uses heat, primers and DNA polymerase to amplify section of DNA, producing many copies from small amount\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul Gel Electrophoresis Process:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Take DNA master sample made during PCR and micropipette it into wells of gel\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Agarose gel acts as mesh wall for DNA move through\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}When loading DNA into wells, don't puncture bottom or overflow top - process won't work\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Place gel with DNA down negatively charged end (DNA negative charged) and fill container with buffer to help produce electrical current\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Machine turned on to allow current move through gel - current is 100V and leave on for 30 mins (otherwise DNA start moving backwards)\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}DNA move through gel to positively charged end - separating depending on size\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Restriction enzymes = ability cut DNA at specific nucleotide sequence\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Cut into different lengths depending on base sequence of specific DNA sample\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul How used for DNA Sequencing:\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\ulnone Size of DNA molecule affect how far along gel they travel, separating into bands\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Ladder present - controlled known source of DNA (pattern/sequence for certain hereditary disease or crime suspect eg)\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Compare unknown source against ladder and check for similarities\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul Looking for Evidence:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Collect DNA\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1 Break open cells and through check cell DNA extraction\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Make lots of copies of DNA fragment\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1 Polymerase chain reaction\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Visualise your DNA\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1 Using gel electrophoresis\par
\par

\pard\fi-720\li720\sl240\slmult1\ul DNA Technology:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1 Genetic engineering = use tech to alter genomes of organisms\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Allows insertion of foreign gene into new cells, able to produce different product\par

\pard\li1136\sl240\slmult1 Biotechnology includes genetic engineering etc make use of natural biological systems achieve end desired by humans\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul Recombinant DNA (rDNA):\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Referred as genetic engineering\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Involve DNA introduction into cells where DNA foreign to organism modified\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Used = take genes from 1 organism and place into another's chromosomes\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Provides potential to replace faulty genes with healthy ones but also potential to identify hereditary diseases\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Technique = isolate and amplify genes/DNA segments and insert into bacterial cells --> creating transgenic bacteria\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Transgenic organisms = genome been altered by transfer of gene(s) from another organism\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}These introduced genes become part organism's DNA and can be passed down\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Process of rDNA:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Isolate the gene of interest\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Gene then inserted into vector and cloned\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Vector now has segment of DNA capable of replicating on its own\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 If gene of interest added to plasmid and then added to vector --> replicate and clone within vector and plasmid --> creating numerous DNA copies to insert into host cells\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Host cell start producing foreign protein, using instructions\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Plasmids (bacteria), viral DNA, retroviruses = vector/host cell\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Genes cloned in recombinant plasmids\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Bacteria take recombinant plasmids and reproduce\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}This clones plasmids and genes they carry\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Products of gene can be harvested\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Biotechnology Products:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Transgenic organisms have foreign gene inserted into them\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Transgenic bacteria\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Insulin, Hepatitis B, promote plant health etc\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Recombinant cells and organisms used manufacture useful proteins\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Gene Therapy:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Aims to treat/cure genetic abnormalities by replacing faulty genes with healthy genes\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Currently used in treatment of single-gene disorders\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Progress slow and ethical limitations\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}DNA carefully selected, correct to effect of mutated gene\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Limited success in treating human diseases\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Different Types:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Somatic\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Transfer DNA section to any cell of body that doesn't produce sperm/eggs\par
Effects of gene therapy not passed down to patient's children\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Germline\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Transfer DNA section to cells producing eggs/sperm\par
Effects of gene therapy passed down to patient's children and subsequent\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Treating Diabetes:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Gene therapy might be used to permanently restore normal blood glucose levels in people with type 1 diabetes\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Reprogrammed glucagon - producing alpha cells in pancreas to produce insulin\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Restore normal blood glucose levels for about 4 months\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Used adeno-associated virus to deliver proteins (Pdx1 and MafA)\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Not tested on humans, only on diabetic mice\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Cell Replacement Therapy:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Stem cells = undifferentiated cells capable of repeated mitotic divisions for long period time - ability to become specialised\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Ideal for producing replacement tissues\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Any disorder involving loss/injury of normal cells --> potential for stem cell replacement therapy\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\ul\par
Cell Replacement Process:\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426\ulnone This type of therapy generated most interest in restoring nervous system - especially due widespread occurence of neurodegenerative disorders\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Eg Parkinson's and Alzheimer's\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Used to:\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Regenerate\par

\pard\fi984\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Identify cues allow regeneration without scarring\par
Like growing a new limb\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Repair\par

\pard\fi984\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Stimulate tissue at cell/molecular level/DNA level to repair itself\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Replace\par

\pard\fi-142\li1846\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Biological substitute created in lab can be implanted to replace tissue/organ of interest\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Parkinson's:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Most attractive method of restoring brain function in Parkinson's is replacement of dying neurons with healthy neuronal tissue\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Healthy tissue surviving and establishing connections with nearby neurons\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Usually using human embryonic stem cells = controversial treatment and ethical debate\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Neuronal transplants\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Remove cells from patient\par
Grow in culture with or without biomaterials\par
Give appropriate chemicals to make cells do what's needed\par
Replace into patient\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\tx426\par
\ul Alzheimer's:\ulnone\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Stem cell therapy able to:\par

\pard\fi416\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Improve functional memory\par
Regenerate neurons\par
Improve overall functional recovery\par
Replace damaged cells with healthy cells\par

\pard{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-360\li720\sl240\slmult1\tx426 Introduce healthy stem cells into body, can find inflammation within body and repair it\par
{\pntext\f1\'B7\tab}Halt progression of disease and regenerate damaged neurons\par
}
